  "accessDecisions": [
    "County Road 45 is the Steele County carry-in at 5218 North County Road 45 below Clinton Falls; it is distinct from Frank Woodfill Wildlife Refuge.",
    "Medford City Park is the Straight River Park landing off 4th Avenue NW. City confirms boating access, but the agency shoreline point is not a resolved ramp edge.",
    "Kroghs Landing is downstream of the former Walcott Mill Dam rapids. Do not call it downstream of the County Road 19 bridge; imagery places the facility south/upstream of that bridge.",
    "Teepee Tonka is a city-confirmed canoe landing near the pedestrian bridge. Keep it distinct from the Bridge-to-Park carry-in farther downstream.",
    "Do not snap facility points onto the river or assign unconfirmed river-bank badges."
  ],
  "distanceDecisions": [
    "Use the 2026 DNR Straight River route table consistently: County Road 45 at 20.8, Medford at 17.1, Kroghs at 10.1, Teepee Tonka at 2.0; river miles decrease downstream.",
    "Retain GIS differences: Medford inventory says 17.2 and Teepee Tonka says 1.8. These do not justify changing the source coordinates or hiding an approximate access map.",
    "Published planning miles remain independent of measured course length; no timing distance adoption."
  ],
